<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Macky Ruiz" canonicalPath="/about/">
  <div class="container page-body">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <img class="about-avatar" src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/supermaru-logo-screenshot.png" alt="SuperMaru logo: illustrated portrait of Macky Ruiz" />
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">I'm Macky Ruiz, an IT professional working across networking, virtualization, automation, security, and IT operations.</p>

      <h2>Background</h2>
      <p>I started SuperMaru in 2014 as a place to share the knowledge and tricks I've picked up along the way in my career. Most of it came from the lab: VMware ESXi and vCenter, Linux servers and storage, and the networking that ties them together.</p>
      <p>I first went through the Cisco Networking Academy in 2011 and kept learning through community college courses in ethical hacking, VMware, and network security, along with certifications from Cisco, AWS, VMware, CompTIA, and ITIL. The details are on my <a href="/resume/">resume</a>.</p>

      <h2>Interests</h2>
      <p>Homelabs on a budget, offensive security and CTFs, cloud security, and automating the repetitive parts of infrastructure. Outside of IT I <a href="https://www.strava.com/athletes/10766256">run</a>, cook, and <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/134256796-macky-ruiz">read</a> a lot. Online I also go by Pidgey Adobo, a gamer handle that mixes Pokémon with the Filipino dish adobo.</p>

      <h2>Lately</h2>
      <p>A YouTube series on building practical homelabs from old laptops, and hallway-con conversations at BSidesLV and DEF CON.</p>

      <p class="muted about-note">The views and opinions expressed on this site are my own and do not reflect the views and opinions of my employer.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
